# [[.Name]]

[[.Title]]: [[.Summary]]. Generated by kickhub from `[[.Template]]` v[[.Version]], target **[[.Target]]**.

## Layout

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `internal/api` | The routes, as a plain `net/http` handler. Add yours here. |
| `cmd/server` | Runs the handler as a normal HTTP server (`make run`) |
[[ if eq .Target "aws" -]]
| `cmd/lambda` | Adapts the handler to a Lambda function URL |
| `infra/` | Lambda, function URL, role and log group |
[[- else if eq .Target "gcp" -]]
| `function.go` | Registers the handler as the Cloud Functions entry point |
| `infra/` | Cloud Function, source bucket and service account |
[[- else -]]
| `docker-compose.yml` | The handler in a container on port 8080 |
[[- end ]]
| `.kickhub.yaml` | Records the template, version and parameters used |

## Run it

```sh
make test
make run          # http://localhost:8080/hello/world
```
[[ if eq .Target "local" ]]
```sh
make up && make smoke
make down
```
[[ else ]]
```sh
make infra-apply                       # builds, then deploys
terraform -chdir=infra output -raw url
```

The function is private by default. Pass `-var public=true` to terraform to open it to anyone with the URL.
[[ end ]]